sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 4 of the command development pipeline (feature-flow sections 3 and 4). It continues the one PR that stage 1 opened as a draft with the spec. The code and the runnable proof cases of the command are pushed to the same branch, so a reviewer can check that the chart, the docs, the cases, the code and the proof cases match. There is one CI: the fast checks plus, for command code, the proof CI (proof:run for the affected commands). It runs on every push. When everything is green the PR leaves draft; then comes the gate, and Swamp adds the PR to the merge queue with a Gateway-minted App token. The merge queue requires the one CI result. The Gateway only admits and mints. GitHub auto-merge is not used.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 4 · code, proof CI and merge in the same PR
  %% kind: pipeline.4-pr-and-ci
  autonumber
  %% lane AG icon=terminal pill=author tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=PR tone=purple
  %% lane CI icon=workflow pill=checks tone=amber
  participant AG as Task VM<br/>author · reviewer
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>authorizes only
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>owns flow · state
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>PR · merge queue
  participant CI as CI<br/>fast · proof CI
  AG->>GH: Push code and proof cases<br/>same branch as the draft PR
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the draft PR of stage 1 exists and its first commit holds the spec: chart, page and cases
  %%> - the cases passed on the nested fleet (stage 3)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pushes the command code and the runnable proof cases to the branch of the draft PR; no second PR is opened
  %%> - the chart, page, cases, code and proof cases are now in one PR, so a reviewer can check that they match
  %%> Not built:
  %%> - PRs opened by the App; today the author opens the draft PR as `nckrtl`
  GH->>CI: Start CI<br/>on the PR head, every push
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - GitHub runs `ci.yml` for the PR head on every push, also while the PR is a draft; there is one CI, and the merge queue requires its one result
  Note over CI: Scope the change<br/>changed files pick the jobs
  %%> Rules:
  %%> - documentation only (`docs/`, `*.md`, charts): docs checks only, never the proof CI; this is the spec commit alone
  %%> - Gateway code: fast checks and the Gateway Pest suite
  %%> - web or CLI code: fast checks and that build
  %%> - command code (workflows, extensions, playbooks, roles, versions): fast checks and the proof CI
  Note over CI: Fast checks<br/>about 1 minute
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs the required job set `Required checks`; every main commit also builds the web artifact and `Gateway release inputs` for the release (stage 5)
  opt command code changed
    opt the PR is from outside
      GH->>CI: Review + run-proofs label<br/>maintainer
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - a maintainer approves the head and adds the label `run-proofs`; the workflow passes that head SHA to `proof:run`
      %%> Why:
      %%> - a new push removes the label; the new head needs a new approval
    end
    CI->>GW: Run the proof CI<br/>proof:run COMMIT
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a job on the beast or shark runner passes only the full SHA and an idempotency key; it checks out nothing and chooses no cases
    %%> - the Gateway checks the commit, selects the cases and starts one Swamp run, as in the chart of `proof:run`
    %%> - the run starts a fresh task VM from the current images, syncs the commit, converges that VM once when the PR changes playbooks or pins, and takes `base`; each batch restores `base` once, nothing converges again
    %%> - the base images stay as they are; only the merge and the seed refresh (stage 6) change them
    %%> Not built:
    %%> - the CI job that calls `proof:run`, and the proof CI as a job of the one CI result; today the queue needs `Required checks` alone
    GW-->>CI: Verdict per case
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the job reads the operation until it ends; a missing result or a failed assertion fails the CI result
  end
  alt every check passes
    CI-->>GH: One CI result<br/>green
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the merge queue requires this one result
    GW->>SW: Admit the ready step<br/>token key name
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - authorizes the step and mints a short-lived App token
    %%> When:
    %%> - the PR is a draft and its CI is green on the head
    SW->>GH: Take the PR out of draft<br/>as the Orbit App
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - marks the PR ready for review with the App token, passed by vault key name
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a draft means the work is still moving; leaving draft says the spec, code and proof cases are done
    %%> Not built:
    %%> - Swamp leaving draft; today the author runs `gh pr ready` as `nckrtl`
    alt manual mode
      GW->>GH: Read the PR reviews<br/>short poll · approval on head
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - Nick's approving review on the exact PR head is the gate; the Gateway sees it with a token that has only `pull_requests: read`
      %%> Why:
      %%> - the Gateway is private and its App receives no webhooks, so a short poll sees the approval
      %%> - a push moves the PR head, so the approval must follow the last push
      %%> Not built:
      %%> - the approval-triggered continuation
      GH-->>GW: Approval on the head
    else automatic mode
      SW->>AG: Final self-review<br/>fresh review agent
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - a new review agent, which took no part in the spec, the code or the earlier reviews, reads the whole PR head and the CI result
      %%> Result:
      %%> - findings go back to the author agent, which fixes them; the new head gets a new CI run and a new review
      AG-->>SW: Pass<br/>or findings
    end
    GW->>SW: Admit the merge step<br/>fresh token key name
    %%> Why:
    %%> - a token lives one hour and an approval can take longer, so the Gateway mints a new one for this step
    SW->>GH: Add to the merge queue<br/>enqueuePullRequest (App token)
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - Swamp adds the PR to the merge queue through GitHub's `enqueuePullRequest` GraphQL mutation, with the Gateway-minted App token passed by vault key name
    %%> - the Orbit App, through this Swamp step, decides whether the PR may merge; the PR's CI is already green and the gate has passed
    %%> History:
    %%> - GitHub auto-merge is no longer used
    %%> Not built:
    %%> - Swamp adding the PR to the merge queue; today the author runs `gh pr merge --auto` as `nckrtl` (the interim)
    %%> - the repository's auto-merge setting is switched off once Swamp enqueues PRs
    GH->>CI: Test the combined commit<br/>merge queue run
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the queue builds the PR on top of the newest main and runs CI again with the same selection rule
    %%> - a batch needs the proof CI only for PRs that change command code
    CI-->>GH: Combined commit green
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the queue run tested the exact commit it now puts on main
    Note over GH: Land the PR<br/>merge queue
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the spec, the code and the proof cases are on main together; the Gateway release (stage 5) finds them
  else a check fails
    CI--xGH: One CI result<br/>red
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the PR stays a draft and out of the queue; the author fixes and pushes again, and CI runs again on the new head
    %%> - a PR that left draft and then goes red is fixed the same way, and the gate starts again on the new head
    %%> - a red combined commit removes the PR from the queue
  end
